nodes.body:
I've flipped the condition :+1:, eae634f3f981f007f0165ab222be71b97abc6936

To make the decision on whether the condition should be true I cycled through versions of `llc` until the code output looked correct using the following code snippet you provided;

```llvm
define float @bfloat_to_f32(bfloat %x) local_unnamed_addr #0 {
    %result = fpext bfloat %x to float
    ret float %result
}

define bfloat @f32_to_bfloat(float %x) local_unnamed_addr #0 {
    %result = fptrunc float %x to bfloat
    ret bfloat %result
}
```

However if we use the following snippet, as the arbiter, then we can use a lower version number;

```llvm
define bfloat @identity(float %x) local_unnamed_addr #0 {
    ret bfloat %x
}
```
Unless I'm missing something, I'd feel somewhat hesitant to call a successful compilation of that snippet a reliable indicator for `has_reliable_f16b`.

